# Auto detect text files and perform LF normalization
* text=auto

# Audio and video are committed as ordinary files and served directly by
# GitHub Pages. Do not put them back under Git LFS: GitHub Pages does not serve
# LFS content at all. It returns the ~130 byte pointer file with a 200 status,
# the browser cannot decode that as media, and the presentation in /digital
# hangs forever waiting for a video that will never become ready.
#
# Keep every file under GitHub's 100 MiB hard limit. Re-encode rather than
# reaching for LFS.
#
# The -text markers also stop the "* text=auto" rule above from ever applying
# line-ending normalisation to a binary file.
*.mp3 -text
*.mp4 -text
*.m4a -text
*.mov -text
*.ogg -text
*.wav -text
*.webm -text
